{"stem": "simple_amp_sequencer", "name": "simple_amp_sequencer", "description": "Simple amplitude sequencer \u2014 applies beat-indexed gain steps to audio.\n\nConsumes a routed `beat` event from an upstream `conductor` (via the public\n`beat_input` event pin) and uses `beat_in_measure` to compute the beat\nposition within a measure, then selects one of four gain values\n(gain_0..gain_3) to scale the audio input.  This creates a simple rhythmic\namplitude pattern that cycles every `beats_per_measure` beats.\n\nBlock arguments:\n  %audio_in \u2014 mono audio input to scale\n\nControl inputs (patchbay-routable):\n  beat_input        \u2014 (event_void, subtype \"beat\") upstream beat trigger;\n                      wire `conductor.beat` -> `simple_amp_sequencer.beat_input`\n\nParameters:\n  bpm               \u2014 tempo in beats per minute (default 120)\n  beats_per_measure \u2014 time signature numerator (default 4)\n  gain_0            \u2014 gain for beat 0 (downbeat, default 1.0)\n  gain_1            \u2014 gain for beat 1 (default 0.5)\n  gain_2            \u2014 gain for beat 2 (default 0.75)\n  gain_3            \u2014 gain for beats 3+ (default 0.25)\n\nThe gain selection uses a 4-step sequencer:\n  beat_in_measure == 0 \u2192 gain_0\n  beat_in_measure == 1 \u2192 gain_1\n  beat_in_measure == 2 \u2192 gain_2\n  beat_in_measure >= 3 \u2192 gain_3\n\nThis graph no longer owns an internal metronome: there is a single\nauthoritative timing source, the upstream conductor, routed in through\n`beat_input`.  `bpm` is retained because the beat *count* (and hence the\nbeat-in-measure index that drives gain selection) is derived locally from\n`crag.curframe` and the beat period; patch the sequencer's `bpm` to match the\nconductor's tempo so the local count tracks the routed beats.", "sr": 48000, "ch": 1, "build_meta": {"gen_datetime": "2026-07-03 04:39 UTC", "git_commit": "3e2993a", "compiled_with": "3e2993a"}, "wasm": "simple_amp_sequencer.wasm", "meta_file": "simple_amp_sequencer.wasm.cragmeta", "meta": {"schema_version": 1, "sample_rate": 48000, "channels": 1, "parameters": [{"name": "loop", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "default": 1.0, "float_index": 0}, {"name": "bpm", "type": "float", "min": 20.0, "max": 300.0, "default": 120.0, "unit": "bpm", "float_index": 1}, {"name": "beats_per_measure", "type": "int", "min": 1, "max": 32, "default": 4, "int_index": 0}, {"name": "gain_0", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 2.0, "default": 1.0, "float_index": 2}, {"name": "gain_1", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 2.0, "default": 0.5, "float_index": 3}, {"name": "gain_2", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 2.0, "default": 0.75, "float_index": 4}, {"name": "gain_3", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 2.0, "default": 0.25, "float_index": 5}], "samplers": ["audio"], "texture_samplers": [], "events": [{"name": "start", "type": "void", "void_index": 0}, {"name": "stop", "type": "void", "void_index": 1}, {"name": "beat_input", "type": "void", "subtype": "beat", "void_index": 2}], "meters": [{"name": "progress", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 0}, {"name": "Output", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 1}], "has_visualizer": true, "has_audio_output": true, "viz_width": 512, "viz_height": 256, "compiled_with": "3e2993a"}, "mca": {"graph": "simple_amp_sequencer", "block_size": 512, "results": [{"label": "Intel Haswell (x86-64-v3)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "haswell", "arch": "x86-64", "ipc": 0.4392, "block_rthroughput": 105.25, "cycles_per_sample": 0.2056, "insns_per_block": 170, "uops_per_block": 421}, {"label": "Intel Skylake-AVX512 (x86-64-v4)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "skylake-avx512", "arch": "x86-64", "ipc": 0.5073, "block_rthroughput": 69.5, "cycles_per_sample": 0.1357, "insns_per_block": 168, "uops_per_block": 417}, {"label": "AMD Zen 3 (znver3)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "znver3", "ar